{"cid": "UgyZf3GFJX1E9y1-Ui14AaABAg", "text": "What goggles do you think are best right now for someone starting in fpv. there’s so much news about the new goggles coming to the market soon but that’s a couple months from now and I want to start flying now. What’s your opinion?", "time": "3 years ago", "author": "@evansamson2703", "channel": "UCyIZZXXnZWVZ7zMFsfgu9Iw", "votes": "2", "replies": "4", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/BbYo2LSTs8U9w2UEOYZSfF-X4Hu5ZVpIZxLCc4f0s-IR0zFLG4sMJdeVMp_pveZBRLWOpSIFEg=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": true, "reply": false, "time_parsed": 1672262506.9042}
{"cid": "UgyZf3GFJX1E9y1-Ui14AaABAg.9bXd6-JCLv99bXfvMFXiJE", "text": "Hey Evan, there's a lot coming out, but it's untested and we don't know if it's going to be good enough. We'd recommend picking up a pair of used DJI FPV v2 goggles, you can find them at a decent price. They've proven themselves, and you'll be set for the next several years! You can also do an easy mod on them to fly analog drones as well.", "time": "3 years ago", "author": "@easydrone3100", "channel": "UCPR3lrm6FYT581pIpkWdP5A", "votes": "1", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/hnKnZQifJkJ-8vA7ZqomHWtzZKlCkUVgbwkHH6sLj3Z5Z2X_BBo8NftYNtxofAfDe0_n-Xsc=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": true, "time_parsed": 1672262507.106878}
